// Topography traced from real elevation data by Wikimedia Commons user
// Milenioscuro ("Mapa de Colombia (orografía)", CC BY-SA 3.0) — kept close
// to the original file: the sea's fill was retinted to the site's palette,
// its own opaque background rect was dropped (this component draws its own
// backdrop behind the neighbouring-country context instead, since the
// original one would otherwise paint over them), and the Inkscape editor
// metadata was stripped to shrink the file. The Bogotá marker, the
// neighbouring-country shape and the small "Colombia within the Americas"
// locator are this site's own addition, styled from tokens.css; their
// outlines come from Natural Earth's public-domain admin-0 boundaries
// (simplified, no attribution required). The five neighbouring countries
// are dissolved into one shape (via GDAL/SQLite ST_Union) so their shared
// borders with each other don't appear as a second, slightly misaligned
// line next to Colombia's own — only the outer coastline/border matters
// here. All positions share one calibrated projection: the pixel bounds of
// Colombia's own outline in the Wikimedia file were matched against its
// real lon/lat bounding box (from Natural Earth) to derive a linear
// lon/lat → pixel transform, then checked against Bogotá's real
// coordinates (4.7110°N, 74.0721°W) and the neighbouring countries' own
// shapes before use.
// Source: https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mapa_de_Colombia_(orograf%C3%ADa).svg
